% UC OSPO Network outputs
%
% One entry per public output of the Network: lessons, software and data,
% talks and workshops, papers, and press. outputs.qmd renders this file through
% scripts/build_outputs.py. references.bib is a separate file: it holds the works
% that the history book and the slides cite.
%
% How to add an entry
%   - Key: <firstauthor><year><shortname>, for example dennis2026ucopen.
%   - The first word in `keywords` picks the section on the page:
%     lesson, software, talk, paper or press. Other keywords follow it.
%   - `date` is ISO: 2026-04-22, 2026-04, or a range such as 2026-08-27/2026-08-28.
%     Entries sort newest first inside each section. Give only the precision you know.
%   - Use the DOI when one exists, and copy it from the Zenodo or publisher record.
%   - Check authors against the record. Zenodo sometimes reverses family and given names.
%
% Checked 2026-11-16: every DOI resolves and its title and authors match the record;
% every URL returned 200, except the CNI page, which refuses automated requests.
%
% 2026-11-18: reconciled against a public-source import covering 2024-11-16 to
% 2026-11-16. Event entries below were checked against their host pages. Routine
% campus meetups stay on https://ucospo.net/events/ and are not listed here.

